IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: sections 131 and 132 -- THE REGISTERED OFFICE AND THE REGISTERED AGENT: who may be the
-- agent, what the agent must do and be, the communications contact, the Secretary of State's and the Court of Chancery's powers over
-- agents, and what happens to a corporation whose agent is enjoined.
--
-- SEAT: a director or officer of a corporation (it must have an office and an agent, and tell the agent whom to contact); an incorporator
-- choosing an agent; an officer or director of an entity that acts as registered agent for others. The Secretary of State, the Court of
-- Chancery and the registered agent get no seat: their acts are encoded as what they mean to the corporation and its people.
-- Cross-references taken as inputs: section 502 and 8 Del. C. chapter 5 generally (not among the inputs), the Secretary's regulations on
-- identity verification, section 136 (this piece, module dg2-registered-agent-changes), section 321 (piece dg10).
-- The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).

§ `Section 131: the registered office`

-- "Every corporation shall have and maintain in this State a registered office which may, but need not be, a place of the corporation's
-- business in this State." For a corporation not organized under this chapter the subsection does not say.
-- src:296 | (a) Every corporation shall have and maintain in this State a registered office which may, but need not be, a place of the corporation’s business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 131(a) (src:296)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(a) the corporation must have and maintain a registered office in this State` `the corporation is organized under this chapter` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is organized under this chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:296 | which may, but need not be, a place of the corporation’s business in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 131(a) (src:296)
GIVEN `the registered office is a place of the corporation's business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(a) the registered office may be a place of the corporation's business in this State` `the registered office is a place of the corporation's business in this State` MEANS
    TRUE

-- "As used in this title, 'registered office' means the address of the registered agent located in this State being appointed to accept
-- service of process and otherwise perform the duties of a registered agent." The address, if it is in this State; otherwise the text does not say.
-- src:297 | (b) As used in this title, “registered office” means the address of the registered agent located in this State being appointed to accept service of process and otherwise perform the duties of a registered agent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 131(b) (src:297)
GIVEN `the address of the registered agent` IS A STRING
      `the address of the registered agent is located in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 131(b) the registered office` `the address of the registered agent` `the address of the registered agent is located in this State` MEANS
    IF   `the address of the registered agent is located in this State`
    THEN JUST `the address of the registered agent`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "As contained in any certificate of incorporation or other document filed with the Secretary of State under this chapter, the address of a
-- registered office shall include the street, number, city, county and postal code."
-- src:298 | (c) As contained in any certificate of incorporation or other document filed with the Secretary of State under this chapter, the address of a registered office shall include the street, number, city, county and postal code.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 131(c) (src:298)
GIVEN `the address includes the street` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address includes the number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address includes the city` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address includes the county` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address includes the postal code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 131(c) the address of the registered office as contained in the filed document is complete` `the address includes the street` `the address includes the number` `the address includes the city` `the address includes the county` `the address includes the postal code` MEANS
        `the address includes the street`
    AND `the address includes the number`
    AND `the address includes the city`
    AND `the address includes the county`
    AND `the address includes the postal code`

§ `Section 132(a): who may be the registered agent`

-- "Every corporation shall have and maintain in this State a registered agent, which agent may be any of: (1) The corporation itself; (2) An
-- individual resident in this State; (3) A domestic corporation (other than the corporation itself), a domestic partnership (whether general
-- (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic limited liability
-- company or a domestic statutory trust; or (4) A foreign corporation, a foreign limited liability partnership, a foreign limited
-- partnership, a foreign limited liability limited partnership, a foreign limited liability company or a foreign statutory trust."
-- The list is closed ("may be any of"). A foreign general partnership that is not a limited liability partnership is not in paragraph
-- (4), and a business trust, a real estate investment trust, a common-law trust or any other unincorporated business is in neither (3) nor (4).
-- "Domestic" is formed under the laws of this State; "foreign" is formed under the laws of any other jurisdiction (core `Where an entity is formed`).
-- src:302 | (a) Every corporation shall have and maintain in this State a registered agent, which agent may be any of:
-- src:303 | (1) The corporation itself;
-- src:304 | (2) An individual resident in this State;
-- src:305 | (3) A domestic corporation (other than the corporation itself), a domestic partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic limited liability company or a domestic statutory trust; or
-- src:306 | (4) A foreign corporation, a foreign limited liability partnership, a foreign limited partnership, a foreign limited liability limited partnership, a foreign limited liability company or a foreign statutory trust.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(a) (src:302-306)
GIVEN `the kind of candidate` IS A `Kind of entity`
      `where the candidate is formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
      `the individual is resident in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(a) the candidate may be the registered agent of the corporation` `the kind of candidate` `where the candidate is formed` `the individual is resident in this State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of candidate`
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN `the individual is resident in this State`
    WHEN `a corporation` k THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a general partnership` THEN `where the candidate is formed` EQUALS `this State`
    WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory trust` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `Section 132(b): what every registered agent must do`

DECLARE `s 132(b) Facts about a registered agent` HAS
    `the agent is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent, an entity, maintains a business office in this State which is generally open at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent, an individual, is generally present at a designated location in this State at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent is a foreign entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent is authorized to transact business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent accepts service of process and other communications directed to the corporations it serves and forwards them to the corporation to which the service or communication is directed` IS A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: section 502 (8 Del. C. ch. 5, not among the inputs): the annual report is theirs; whether the agent forwards it is a plain fact.
    `the agent forwards to the corporations it serves the annual report required by section 502 or an electronic notification of it in a form satisfactory to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent satisfies and adheres to the regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which the agent maintains a record` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Every registered agent for a domestic corporation or a foreign corporation shall: a. If an entity, maintain a business office in this
-- State which is generally open, or if an individual, be generally present at a designated location in this State, at sufficiently
-- frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent; b. If a foreign entity, be
-- authorized to transact business in this State; c. Accept service of process and other communications directed to the corporations for
-- which it serves as registered agent and forward same to the corporation to which the service or communication is directed; d. Forward to
-- the corporations for which it serves as registered agent the annual report required by § 502 of this title or an electronic
-- notification of same in a form satisfactory to the Secretary of State ('Secretary'); and e. Satisfy and adhere to regulations
-- established by the Secretary regarding the verification of both the identity of the entity's contacts and individuals for which the
-- registered agent maintains a record for the reduction of risk of unlawful business purposes." The duty of the agent, the claim of the corporation.
-- src:307 | (b) (1) Every registered agent for a domestic corporation or a foreign corporation shall:
-- src:308 | a. If an entity, maintain a business office in this State which is generally open, or if an individual, be generally present at a designated location in this State, at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent;
-- src:309 | b. If a foreign entity, be authorized to transact business in this State;
-- src:310 | c. Accept service of process and other communications directed to the corporations for which it serves as registered agent and forward same to the corporation to which the service or communication is directed;
-- src:311 | d. Forward to the corporations for which it serves as registered agent the annual report required by § 502 of this title or an electronic notification of same in a form satisfactory to the Secretary of State (“Secretary”); and
-- src:312 | e. Satisfy and adhere to regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of both the identity of the entity’s contacts and individuals for which the registered agent maintains a record for the reduction of risk of unlawful business purposes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(b)(1) (src:307-312)
GIVEN f IS A `s 132(b) Facts about a registered agent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(b)(1) the registered agent has done what the Law requires of every registered agent` f MEANS
        (IF   f's `the agent is an individual`
         THEN f's `the agent, an individual, is generally present at a designated location in this State at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent`
         ELSE f's `the agent, an entity, maintains a business office in this State which is generally open at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent`)
    AND (   (NOT f's `the agent is a foreign entity`)
         OR f's `the agent is authorized to transact business in this State`)
    AND f's `the agent accepts service of process and other communications directed to the corporations it serves and forwards them to the corporation to which the service or communication is directed`
    AND f's `the agent forwards to the corporations it serves the annual report required by section 502 or an electronic notification of it in a form satisfactory to the Secretary of State`
    AND f's `the agent satisfies and adheres to the regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which the agent maintains a record`

-- "A registered agent may not perform its duties or functions solely through the use of a virtual office, the retention by the agent of a
-- mail forwarding service, or both. For purposes of this paragraph (b)(2), 'virtual office' means the performance of duties or functions
-- solely through the internet or solely through other means of remote communication."
-- src:313 | (2) A registered agent may not perform its duties or functions solely through the use of a virtual office, the retention by the agent of a mail forwarding service, or both. For purposes of this paragraph (b)(2), “virtual office” means the performance of duties or functions solely through the internet or solely through other means of remote communication.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(b)(2) (src:313)
GIVEN `the agent performs duties or functions solely through the internet or solely through other means of remote communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent retains a mail forwarding service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent performs any duty or function in any other way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(b)(2) the registered agent may perform its duties or functions in this way` `the agent performs duties or functions solely through the internet or solely through other means of remote communication` `the agent retains a mail forwarding service` `the agent performs any duty or function in any other way` MEANS
    NOT (   (   `the agent performs duties or functions solely through the internet or solely through other means of remote communication`
             OR `the agent retains a mail forwarding service`)
         AND (NOT `the agent performs any duty or function in any other way`))

§ `Section 132(c): the commercial registered agent`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 132(c) the number of entities above which an agent is a commercial registered agent` MEANS 50

-- "Any registered agent who at any time serves as registered agent for more than 50 entities (a 'commercial registered agent'), whether
-- domestic or foreign" and (c)(3): "a commercial registered agent shall also include any registered agent which has an officer, director
-- or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents if such registered agents at any time during such common service
-- as officer, director or managing agent collectively served as registered agents for more than 50 entities, whether domestic or
-- foreign." "More than 50" is strict: 50 is not enough, 51 is.
-- src:314 | (c) Any registered agent who at any time serves as registered agent for more than 50 entities (a “commercial registered agent”), whether domestic or foreign, shall satisfy and comply with the following qualifications.
-- src:327 | (3) For purposes of this subsection and paragraph (f)(2)a. of this section, a commercial registered agent shall also include any registered agent which has an officer, director or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents if such registered agents at any time during such common service as officer, director or managing agent collectively served as registered agents for more than 50 entities, whether domestic or foreign.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(c) (src:314); § 132(c)(3) (src:327)
GIVEN `the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which the agent serves as registered agent at any one time` IS A NUMBER
      `the agent has an officer, director or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which the agents with that officer, director or managing agent in common collectively served as registered agents at any time during that common service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(c) the registered agent is a commercial registered agent` `the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which the agent serves as registered agent at any one time` `the agent has an officer, director or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents` `the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which the agents with that officer, director or managing agent in common collectively served as registered agents at any time during that common service` MEANS
        (`the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which the agent serves as registered agent at any one time` GREATER THAN `s 132(c) the number of entities above which an agent is a commercial registered agent`)
    OR (    `the agent has an officer, director or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents`
        AND (`the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which the agents with that officer, director or managing agent in common collectively served as registered agents at any time during that common service` GREATER THAN `s 132(c) the number of entities above which an agent is a commercial registered agent`))

DECLARE `s 132(c) Facts about a commercial registered agent` HAS
    `the agent is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent maintains a principal residence or a principal place of business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent has a business office within this State which is generally open during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent maintains a Delaware business license` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent, a natural person, is generally present at a designated location within this State during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an officer, director or managing agent who is a natural person is generally present at the office during normal business hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent provides the Secretary upon request with the information identifying and enabling communication with the agent that the Secretary requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent satisfies and adheres to the regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which it maintains a record` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (c)(1), a natural person: a. principal residence or principal place of business in this State; b. a Delaware business license; c. generally
-- present at a designated location in this State during normal business hours; d. provide the Secretary on request with the identifying
-- information; e. adhere to the Secretary's regulations. (c)(2), a corporation, partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust,
-- domestic or foreign: a. a business office within this State generally open during normal business hours; b. a Delaware business license;
-- c. generally present at the office during normal business hours an officer, director or managing agent who is a natural person; d. and e. as
-- for a natural person.
-- src:315 | (1) A natural person serving as a commercial registered agent shall:
-- src:316 | a. Maintain a principal residence or a principal place of business in this State;
-- src:317 | b. Maintain a Delaware business license;
-- src:318 | c. Be generally present at a designated location within this State during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b) of this section;
-- src:319 | d. Provide the Secretary upon request with such information identifying and enabling communication with such commercial registered agent as the Secretary shall require; and
-- src:320 | e. Satisfy and adhere to regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of both the identity of the entity’s contacts and individuals for which the natural person maintains a record for the reduction of risk of unlawful business purposes.
-- src:321 | (2) A domestic or foreign corporation, a domestic or foreign partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic or foreign limited liability company, or a domestic or foreign statutory trust serving as a commercial registered agent shall:
-- src:322 | a. Have a business office within this State which is generally open during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b) of this section;
-- src:323 | b. Maintain a Delaware business license;
-- src:324 | c. Have generally present at such office during normal business hours an officer, director or managing agent who is a natural person;
-- src:325 | d. Provide the Secretary upon request with such information identifying and enabling communication with such commercial registered agent as the Secretary shall require; and
-- src:326 | e. Satisfy and adhere to regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of both the identity of the entity’s contacts and individuals for which it maintains a record for the reduction of risk of unlawful business purposes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(c)(1) (src:315-320); § 132(c)(2) (src:321-326)
GIVEN f IS A `s 132(c) Facts about a commercial registered agent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(c) the commercial registered agent meets the qualifications` f MEANS
        (IF   f's `the agent is a natural person`
         THEN     f's `the agent maintains a principal residence or a principal place of business in this State`
              AND f's `the agent, a natural person, is generally present at a designated location within this State during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b)`
         ELSE     f's `the agent has a business office within this State which is generally open during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b)`
              AND f's `an officer, director or managing agent who is a natural person is generally present at the office during normal business hours`)
    AND f's `the agent maintains a Delaware business license`
    AND f's `the agent provides the Secretary upon request with the information identifying and enabling communication with the agent that the Secretary requires`
    AND f's `the agent satisfies and adheres to the regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which it maintains a record`

-- An agent that is not a commercial registered agent is not subject to subsection (c): in compliance.
-- src:314 | (c) Any registered agent who at any time serves as registered agent for more than 50 entities (a “commercial registered agent”), whether domestic or foreign, shall satisfy and comply with the following qualifications.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(c) (src:314)
GIVEN `the registered agent is a commercial registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commercial registered agent meets the qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(c) the registered agent is in compliance with subsection (c)` `the registered agent is a commercial registered agent` `the commercial registered agent meets the qualifications` MEANS
        (NOT `the registered agent is a commercial registered agent`)
    OR  `the commercial registered agent meets the qualifications`

§ `Section 132(d): the communications contact`

DECLARE `s 132(d) Facts about the communications contact` HAS
    `the corporation is formed under the laws of this State or qualified to do business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the name of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the business address of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the business telephone number of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a natural person who is an officer, director, employee, or designated agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is then authorized to receive communications from the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has updated the information from time to time as necessary` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Every corporation formed under the laws of this State or qualified to do business in this State shall provide to its registered agent and
-- update from time to time as necessary the name, business address and business telephone number of a natural person who is an officer,
-- director, employee, or designated agent of the corporation, who is then authorized to receive communications from the registered agent.
-- Such person shall be deemed the communications contact for the corporation." A corporation neither formed nor qualified here: not covered.
-- src:328 | Every corporation formed under the laws of this State or qualified to do business in this State shall provide to its registered agent and update from time to time as necessary the name, business address and business telephone number of a natural person who is an officer, director, employee, or designated agent of the corporation, who is then authorized to receive communications from the registered agent. Such person shall be deemed the communications contact for the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(d) (src:328)
GIVEN f IS A `s 132(d) Facts about the communications contact`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(d) the corporation has provided the registered agent with a communications contact as the Law requires` f MEANS
    IF   NOT f's `the corporation is formed under the laws of this State or qualified to do business in this State`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (   f's `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the name of the person`
              AND f's `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the business address of the person`
              AND f's `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the business telephone number of the person`
              AND f's `the person is a natural person who is an officer, director, employee, or designated agent of the corporation`
              AND f's `the person is then authorized to receive communications from the registered agent`
              AND f's `the corporation has updated the information from time to time as necessary`)

-- "Every registered agent shall retain (in paper or electronic form) the above information concerning the current communications contact for
-- each corporation for which such agent serves as a registered agent."
-- src:328 | Every registered agent shall retain (in paper or electronic form) the above information concerning the current communications contact for each corporation for which such agent serves as a registered agent. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(d) (src:328)
GIVEN `the agent retains the information in paper form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent retains the information in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(d) the registered agent retains the information about the communications contact as the Law requires` `the agent retains the information in paper form` `the agent retains the information in electronic form` MEANS
    `the agent retains the information in paper form` OR `the agent retains the information in electronic form`

-- "If the corporation fails to provide the registered agent with a current communications contact, the registered agent may resign as the
-- registered agent for such corporation pursuant to § 136 of this title." The agent's power; the corporation's liability to it.
-- src:328 | If the corporation fails to provide the registered agent with a current communications contact, the registered agent may resign as the registered agent for such corporation pursuant to § 136 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(d) (src:328)
GIVEN `the corporation fails to provide the registered agent with a current communications contact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(d) the registered agent may resign as the registered agent pursuant to section 136` `the corporation fails to provide the registered agent with a current communications contact` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation fails to provide the registered agent with a current communications contact`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 132(e) and (g): the Secretary of State`

-- (e), second sentence: "Such actions may include refusal to file documents submitted by a registered agent, including the refusal to file any
-- documents regarding an entity's formation." The actions are those "reasonable and necessary to assure registered agents' compliance with
-- subsections (b), (c) and (d)". (The Secretary's power to issue regulations, in the first sentence, is machinery and is not encoded.)
-- src:329 | and to take actions reasonable and necessary to assure registered agents’ compliance with subsections (b), (c) and (d) of this section. Such actions may include refusal to file documents submitted by a registered agent, including the refusal to file any documents regarding an entity’s formation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(e) (src:329)
GIVEN `the document is submitted by a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal is reasonable and necessary to assure the registered agent's compliance with subsections (b), (c) and (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(e) the Secretary may refuse to file the document` `the document is submitted by a registered agent` `the refusal is reasonable and necessary to assure the registered agent's compliance with subsections (b), (c) and (d)` MEANS
    IF   `the document is submitted by a registered agent` AND `the refusal is reasonable and necessary to assure the registered agent's compliance with subsections (b), (c) and (d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 132(f): injunction against a registered agent, and the corporation's thirty days`

DECLARE `s 132(f)(2) Facts about the grounds` HAS
    `the latest date on or before the filing of the complaint on which the registered agent was a commercial registered agent` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the Secretary's complaint was filed` IS A DATE
    `the registered agent failed, after notice and warning, to comply with the qualifications in subsection (b) or the requirements of subsection (c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person serving as registered agent, or an officer, director or managing agent of an entity registered agent, has been convicted of a felony or of a crime which includes an element of dishonesty or fraud or involves moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the registered agent has engaged in conduct in connection with acting as a registered agent that is intended to or likely to deceive or defraud the public` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (f)(2): "Any one or more of the following grounds shall be a sufficient basis to grant an injunction pursuant to this section: a. With respect to
-- any registered agent who at any time within 1 year immediately prior to the filing of the Secretary's complaint is a commercial
-- registered agent, failure after notice and warning to comply with the qualifications set forth in subsection (b) of this section and/or
-- the requirements of subsection (c) or (d) of this section above; b. The person serving as a registered agent, or any person who is an
-- officer, director or managing agent of an entity registered agent, has been convicted of a felony or any crime which includes an element
-- of dishonesty or fraud or involves moral turpitude; c. The registered agent has engaged in conduct in connection with acting as a
-- registered agent that is intended to or likely to deceive or defraud the public." A ground is a sufficient basis, not a requirement.
-- src:332 | (2) Any one or more of the following grounds shall be a sufficient basis to grant an injunction pursuant to this section:
-- src:333 | a. With respect to any registered agent who at any time within 1 year immediately prior to the filing of the Secretary’s complaint is a commercial registered agent, failure after notice and warning to comply with the qualifications set forth in subsection (b) of this section and/or the requirements of subsection (c) or (d) of this section above;
-- src:334 | b. The person serving as a registered agent, or any person who is an officer, director or managing agent of an entity registered agent, has been convicted of a felony or any crime which includes an element of dishonesty or fraud or involves moral turpitude;
-- src:335 | c. The registered agent has engaged in conduct in connection with acting as a registered agent that is intended to or likely to deceive or defraud the public.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(2) (src:332-335)
GIVEN f IS A `s 132(f)(2) Facts about the grounds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(f)(2) a ground exists that is a sufficient basis to grant an injunction` f MEANS
        (CONSIDER f's `the latest date on or before the filing of the complaint on which the registered agent was a commercial registered agent`
         WHEN JUST d THEN (    (d AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in years` 1) `before` (f's `the date the Secretary's complaint was filed`)))
                           AND f's `the registered agent failed, after notice and warning, to comply with the qualifications in subsection (b) or the requirements of subsection (c) or (d)`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    OR  f's `the person serving as registered agent, or an officer, director or managing agent of an entity registered agent, has been convicted of a felony or of a crime which includes an element of dishonesty or fraud or involves moral turpitude`
    OR  f's `the registered agent has engaged in conduct in connection with acting as a registered agent that is intended to or likely to deceive or defraud the public`

-- (f): "Upon application of the Secretary, the Court of Chancery may enjoin any person or entity from serving as a registered agent or as an
-- officer, director or managing agent of a registered agent." Without the Secretary's application the Court has no power under this section;
-- with it, and a ground, the Court may; with it and no ground the text does not say.
-- src:330 | (f) Upon application of the Secretary, the Court of Chancery may enjoin any person or entity from serving as a registered agent or as an officer, director or managing agent of a registered agent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f) (src:330)
GIVEN `the Secretary has applied to the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ground exists that is a sufficient basis to grant an injunction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(f) the Court of Chancery may enjoin the person or entity from serving` `the Secretary has applied to the Court of Chancery` `a ground exists that is a sufficient basis to grant an injunction` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the Secretary has applied to the Court of Chancery`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF   `a ground exists that is a sufficient basis to grant an injunction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- (f)(1): "Upon the filing of a complaint by the Secretary pursuant to this section, the Court may make such orders respecting such proceeding
-- as it deems appropriate, and may enter such orders granting interim or final relief as it deems proper under the circumstances." What
-- orders the Court makes is the Court's discretion and is not computed; the rule answers only whether the Court has the power to make them:
-- it has, once the Secretary has filed a complaint pursuant to this section; without one the text does not say.
-- src:331 | (1) Upon the filing of a complaint by the Secretary pursuant to this section, the Court may make such orders respecting such proceeding as it deems appropriate, and may enter such orders granting interim or final relief as it deems proper under the circumstances.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(1) (src:331)
GIVEN `the Secretary has filed a complaint pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(f)(1) the Court may make orders respecting the proceeding and enter orders granting interim or final relief` `the Secretary has filed a complaint pursuant to this section` MEANS
    IF   `the Secretary has filed a complaint pursuant to this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (f)(3), second sentence: "Any person who, on or after January 1, 2007, serves as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity
-- acting as a registered agent in this State shall be deemed thereby to have consented to the appointment of such registered agent as agent
-- upon whom service of process may be made in any action brought pursuant to this section, and service as an officer, director, or managing
-- agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State shall be a signification of the consent of such person that any process when
-- so served shall be of the same legal force and validity as if served upon such person within this State, and such appointment of the
-- registered agent shall be irrevocable." Before that date the text does not say.
-- src:336 | Any person who, on or after January 1, 2007, serves as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State shall be deemed thereby to have consented to the appointment of such registered agent as agent upon whom service of process may be made in any action brought pursuant to this section, and service as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State shall be a signification of the consent of such person that any process when so served shall be of the same legal force and validity as if served upon such person within this State, and such appointment of the registered agent shall be irrevocable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(3) (src:336)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 132(f)(3) January 1, 2007` MEANS YMD 2007 1 1

-- src:336 | Any person who, on or after January 1, 2007, serves as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State shall be deemed thereby to have consented to the appointment of such registered agent as agent upon whom service of process may be made in any action brought pursuant to this section, and service as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State shall be a signification of the consent of such person that any process when so served shall be of the same legal force and validity as if served upon such person within this State, and such appointment of the registered agent shall be irrevocable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(3) (src:336)
GIVEN `the person serves as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the person so serves` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(f)(3) the person is deemed to have consented to the appointment of the registered agent as agent for service of process` `the person serves as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State` `the date on which the person so serves` MEANS
    IF   `the person serves as an officer, director, or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in this State`
         AND (`the date on which the person so serves` AT LEAST `s 132(f)(3) January 1, 2007`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (f)(3), first sentence: "With respect to any order the court enters pursuant to this section with respect to an entity that has acted as a
-- registered agent, the court may also direct such order to any person who has served as an officer, director, or managing agent of such registered agent."
-- src:336 | With respect to any order the court enters pursuant to this section with respect to an entity that has acted as a registered agent, the court may also direct such order to any person who has served as an officer, director, or managing agent of such registered agent. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(3) (src:336)
GIVEN `the order is with respect to an entity that has acted as a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has served as an officer, director, or managing agent of that registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(f)(3) the court may direct the order to the person` `the order is with respect to an entity that has acted as a registered agent` `the person has served as an officer, director, or managing agent of that registered agent` MEANS
    IF   `the order is with respect to an entity that has acted as a registered agent` AND `the person has served as an officer, director, or managing agent of that registered agent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 132 Consequence of failing to designate a new registered agent` IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary of State declares the charter of the domestic corporation forfeited`
    `the Secretary of State forfeits the foreign corporation's qualification or authority to do business in this State`
    `the corporation is not forfeited, because it obtained and designated a new registered agent in time`

DECLARE `s 132(f)(4) Facts about the corporation` HAS
    `where the corporation is formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
    `the Secretary mailed or delivered notice of the order to the corporation at the address of its principal place of business specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
    `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date as of which the question is asked` IS A DATE

-- (f)(4): "Upon the entry of an order by the Court enjoining any person or entity from acting as a registered agent, the Secretary shall mail
-- or deliver notice of such order to each affected corporation at the address of its principal place of business as specified in its most
-- recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary. If such corporation is a domestic corporation and fails to obtain and
-- designate a new registered agent within 30 days after such notice is given, the Secretary shall declare the charter of such corporation
-- forfeited. If such corporation is a foreign corporation, and fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent within 30 days after such
-- notice is given, the Secretary shall forfeit its qualification to do business in this State." The last day is the thirtieth day after
-- notice (core Fork F3); a designation on that day is in time. NOTHING while the thirty days have not run and no agent is designated, and
-- when the notice was not given as the subsection requires (the period has not started).
-- src:337 | Upon the entry of an order by the Court enjoining any person or entity from acting as a registered agent, the Secretary shall mail or deliver notice of such order to each affected corporation at the address of its principal place of business as specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary. If such corporation is a domestic corporation and fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent within 30 days after such notice is given, the Secretary shall declare the charter of such corporation forfeited. If such corporation is a foreign corporation, and fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent within 30 days after such notice is given, the Secretary shall forfeit its qualification to do business in this State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(4) (src:337)
GIVEN f IS A `s 132(f)(4) Facts about the corporation`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 132(f)(4) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` f MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` (f's `the date the notice was given`)

-- src:337 | Upon the entry of an order by the Court enjoining any person or entity from acting as a registered agent, the Secretary shall mail or deliver notice of such order to each affected corporation at the address of its principal place of business as specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary. If such corporation is a domestic corporation and fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent within 30 days after such notice is given, the Secretary shall declare the charter of such corporation forfeited. If such corporation is a foreign corporation, and fails to obtain and designate a new registered agent within 30 days after such notice is given, the Secretary shall forfeit its qualification to do business in this State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(4) (src:337)
GIVEN f IS A `s 132(f)(4) Facts about the corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 132 Consequence of failing to designate a new registered agent`
`s 132(f)(4) what follows for the corporation` f MEANS
    IF   NOT f's `the Secretary mailed or delivered notice of the order to the corporation at the address of its principal place of business specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER f's `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent`
         WHEN JUST d THEN
             IF   d AT MOST `s 132(f)(4) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` f
             THEN JUST `the corporation is not forfeited, because it obtained and designated a new registered agent in time`
             ELSE JUST forfeiture
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF   f's `the date as of which the question is asked` AT MOST `s 132(f)(4) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` f
             THEN NOTHING
             ELSE JUST forfeiture
    WHERE
        forfeiture MEANS
            IF   `the entity was formed under the laws of this State` (Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `a corporation` `a stock corporation`, `where formed` IS f's `where the corporation is formed`)
            THEN `the Secretary of State declares the charter of the domestic corporation forfeited`
            ELSE `the Secretary of State forfeits the foreign corporation's qualification or authority to do business in this State`

-- (f)(4), continued: "If the court enjoins a person or entity from acting as a registered agent as provided in this section and no new
-- registered agent shall have been obtained and designated in the time and manner aforesaid, service of legal process against the
-- corporation for which the registered agent had been acting shall thereafter be upon the Secretary in accordance with § 321 of this title."
-- src:337 | If the court enjoins a person or entity from acting as a registered agent as provided in this section and no new registered agent shall have been obtained and designated in the time and manner aforesaid, service of legal process against the corporation for which the registered agent had been acting shall thereafter be upon the Secretary in accordance with § 321 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(4) (src:337)
GIVEN `the court has enjoined the person or entity from acting as the corporation's registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new registered agent was obtained and designated in the time and manner required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(f)(4) service of legal process against the corporation is upon the Secretary` `the court has enjoined the person or entity from acting as the corporation's registered agent` `a new registered agent was obtained and designated in the time and manner required` MEANS
    IF   `the court has enjoined the person or entity from acting as the corporation's registered agent` AND (NOT `a new registered agent was obtained and designated in the time and manner required`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The Court of Chancery may, upon application of the Secretary on notice to the former registered agent, enter such orders as it deems
-- appropriate to give the Secretary access to information in the former registered agent's possession in order to facilitate
-- communication with the corporations the former registered agent served."
-- src:337 | The Court of Chancery may, upon application of the Secretary on notice to the former registered agent, enter such orders as it deems appropriate to give the Secretary access to information in the former registered agent’s possession in order to facilitate communication with the corporations the former registered agent served.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(f)(4) (src:337)
GIVEN `the Secretary has applied on notice to the former registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(f)(4) the Court of Chancery may order that the Secretary be given access to the former registered agent's information` `the Secretary has applied on notice to the former registered agent` MEANS
    IF   `the Secretary has applied on notice to the former registered agent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 132(h): "resident agent"`

-- "Whenever the term 'resident agent' or 'resident agent in charge of a corporation's principal office or place of business in this State,' or
-- other term of like import which refers to a corporation's agent required by statute to be located in this State, is or has been used in a
-- corporation's certificate of incorporation, or in any other document, or in any statute, it shall be deemed to mean and refer to, unless the
-- context indicates otherwise, the corporation's registered agent required by this section; and it shall not be necessary for any
-- corporation to amend its certificate of incorporation or any other document to comply with this section."
-- src:339 | Whenever the term “resident agent” or “resident agent in charge of a corporation’s principal office or place of business in this State,” or other term of like import which refers to a corporation’s agent required by statute to be located in this State, is or has been used in a corporation’s certificate of incorporation, or in any other document, or in any statute, it shall be deemed to mean and refer to, unless the context indicates otherwise, the corporation’s registered agent required by this section; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(h) (src:339)
GIVEN `the term is “resident agent” or a term of like import which refers to a corporation's agent required by statute to be located in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132(h) the term is deemed to refer to the corporation's registered agent` `the term is “resident agent” or a term of like import which refers to a corporation's agent required by statute to be located in this State` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF   `the term is “resident agent” or a term of like import which refers to a corporation's agent required by statute to be located in this State` AND (NOT `the context indicates otherwise`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:339 | and it shall not be necessary for any corporation to amend its certificate of incorporation or any other document to comply with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 132(h) (src:339)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or another document uses the term “resident agent” or a term of like import` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132(h) the corporation must amend its certificate of incorporation or any other document to comply with section 132` `the certificate of incorporation or another document uses the term “resident agent” or a term of like import` MEANS
    FALSE
